GetIntroductionContent() {
    content := FormatHeader("INTRODUCTION")
    content .= "Welcome to the Ultimate Keyboard Shortcuts System!`n`n"
    content .= "This script provides a quick and easy way to access keyboard shortcuts for a variety of applications and Windows features. `n`n"
    content .= "How to Use:`n"
    content .= "1. Activate the Menu: Press AppsKey + G (or your custom hotkey) to open the main menu.`n"
    content .= "2. Navigate: Use your mouse or arrow keys to browse through the categories and submenus.`n"
    content .= "3. Select a Guide: Click on a specific shortcut guide (e.g., 'Windows Shortcut commands', 'Excel Shortcut commands').`n"
    content .= "4. View Shortcuts: A window will appear displaying the relevant keyboard shortcuts for your selection.`n"
    content .= "5. Close Guide: Click the 'Close' button or press the Escape key to close the shortcut guide window.`n`n"
    content .= "Features:`n"
    content .= "- Comprehensive Lists: Access shortcuts for common Windows operations, Microsoft Office (desktop & online), Google Suite, web browsers, accessibility tools, and more.`n"
    content .= "- Office 365 Online Support: Complete keyboard shortcuts for all Office 365 web applications including Word Online, Excel Online, PowerPoint Online, Outlook Online, OneNote Online, Teams Web, OneDrive Web, and SharePoint Online.`n"
    content .= "- Default Windows Applications: Extensive shortcuts for built-in Windows apps including Calculator, Notepad, WordPad, Paint, Photos, Mail, Calendar, Maps, Settings, Task Manager, Command Prompt, PowerShell, Windows Terminal, Sticky Notes, Voice Recorder, and more.`n"
    content .= "- Modular Design: Easily add new shortcut guides to the system.`n"
    content .= "- Centralized Access: All your essential shortcuts in one place, triggered by a simple hotkey.`n`n"
    content .= "Customization:`n"
    content .= "- Hotkey: You can change the activation hotkey (currently AppsKey + G) by editing the script in the 'HOTKEYS' section near the end.`n"
    content .= "- Adding New Guides: Follow the instructions within the script comments in the InitializeShortcutGuides() function and MenuStructure array to add your own custom shortcut lists.`n`n"
    content .= "We hope this tool enhances your productivity and makes your workflow smoother!`n"
    return content
}

GetModifierKeysContent() {
